{"name":"Java","hex":"#259797","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Java","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 15924  script code for Javanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Pompilidae – certain tarantula wasps."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Java"}],"entries":[{"title":"Java","blocks":[{"text":"Java is one of the Greater Sunda Islands in the South East Asian country of Indonesia. It is bordered by the Indian Ocean to the south and the Java Sea to the north. Java is the world's most populous island, home to an estimated 159.2 million people; about 56% of the Indonesian population, while constituting only 7% of the country's land area. Indonesia's capital city, Jakarta, is located on Java's northwestern coast."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Java_Topography.png/330px-Java_Topography.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java","wikidata":"Q3757"},{"title":"Java (programming language)","blocks":[{"text":"Java is a high-level, general-purpose, memory-safe, object-oriented programming language. It is intended to let programmers write once, run anywhere (WORA), meaning that compiled Java code can run on all platforms that support Java without the need to recompile. Java applications are usually compiled to bytecode that can run on any Java virtual machine (JVM) regardless of the underlying computer architecture. The syntax of Java is similar to C and C++, but has fewer low-level facilities than either of them. The Java runtime provides dynamic abilities usually unavailable in traditional compiled languages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/30/Java_programming_language_logo.svg/330px-Java_programming_language_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java_(programming_language)","wikidata":"Q251"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg/500px-Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg/1280px-Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg/500px-Bromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Bromo in Malang, East Java","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABromo_yang_menakjubkan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg/500px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg/500px-COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parahyangan highland near Buitenzorg (now Bogor, West Java), c. 1865–1872","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_De_weg_van_Buitenzorg_naar_de_Preanger_Regentschappen_TMnr_3728-429c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Cymbidium_dayanum_Orchi_04.jpg/500px-Cymbidium_dayanum_Orchi_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Cymbidium_dayanum_Orchi_04.jpg/500px-Cymbidium_dayanum_Orchi_04.jpg?utm_source